ahmia-crawler on FenrirOS
=========================

Installed but not started; nothing runs by itself. It crawls .onion sites, so read the points below first.

1. Needs Elasticsearch 8 (the index, see ahmia-index). Elasticsearch is not in the repository.
2. Needs the local HTTP proxy pool on localhost:15000-15099, one Tor client behind each. The
   scripts are in /usr/share/ahmia-crawler/torfleet: copy that directory somewhere writable
   (it writes its data, logs and pids next to itself), then run   bash runfleet.sh
   (100 tor + privoxy pairs; edit NUM_INSTANCES for fewer, and change HTTP_PROXY_TOR_PROXIES in
   settings to match). Privoxy's own config in privoxy_configs/ is used instead of /etc/privoxy.
3. Settings: copy /etc/ahmia-crawler/env.example to /etc/ahmia-crawler/env and edit.
4. Run as the ahmia-crawler user:
     su -s /bin/sh ahmia-crawler -c 'ahmia-crawl -s DEPTH_LIMIT=1 -s LOG_LEVEL=DEBUG'
   The upstream daily and monthly schedules are in /usr/share/ahmia-crawler/run_daily.sh,
   run.sh and systemd_examples/ (adapt them to cron/dinit yourself; no job is installed).
